; -*- mode: lisp -*-
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; WHAT EVERY VARIANT SHARES, stated once. The nine documents beside this file
; inherit it: a variant's own :staging clause wins key by key (hammers stands
; in the plain bench with one arm and the plain arrangement, the level-1
; reductions carry their own rig and budget), its :objects and :fixtures are
; added to the fixture below, and its :artifacts stand alone -- the tools
; module is not here because the hammers and the pliers ship none.
;
; The one shared fixture is the pegboard wall. Nothing scores against it, and
; it used to be scenery a loader supplied undeclared; declared here it is
; placed by its own record (skadis_pegboard's build factory) and every
; variant stands in front of the same wall. Every other fixture is a
; variant's own, typed by the station it stands at -- pegboard_hook_wrench_left,
; plier_support_right -- because a record names one placement and the hook
; stands at five; see tasks/tool_hanging/assets/records.py.
;
; MuJoCo integrates the arms; Newton generates the contacts from the CoACD
; hull sets -- a wrench ring is a hole, and a hole survives decomposition
; only as many convex pieces. See tasks/tool_hanging/staging.py for the
; arrangement and the rig, tasks/tool_hanging/scenes.py for the cell.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(define (suite tool_hanging)

  (:language Hang wrenches, scissors and pliers on their pegboard holders, stand
             screwdrivers in a rack, and hang hammers one-armed: geometric hanging
             goals over CoACD compound colliders on the bimanual YAM.)

  (:staging
    (:scene tool_hanging_bench)
    ; The two arms are solid to each other. Each arm stays internally
    ; filtered; see EmbodimentSpec.cross_arm_collisions. Only one arm hangs
    ; anything here and the other parks -- which is exactly the case nothing
    ; was checking, since a parked arm is only out of the way for as long as
    ; something measures that it is. The hammers restate the whole clause
    ; one-armed, arms-solid included.
    (:embodiment yam_tool_hanging (:work-arm left) (:support-arm right) (:arms-solid true))
    (:physics tool_hanging_960hz@v1)
    (:cameras tool_hanging_views@v1)
    (:control-mode joint_position)
    (:episodes (:count 1) (:seed 0) (:sampler fixed))
    ; Every scripted variant lays out an action vector per arm and parks the
    ; idle one, so a one-armed robot is refused at build rather than
    ; discovered mid-rollout. The hammers say (:arms 1) for themselves.
    (:arms 2)
    ; Success ends the episode (the default, so nothing is stated), and a
    ; policy that never asks to stop is scored when the tools are hung rather
    ; than at its step budget. Every goal requires the release for that to be
    ; safe: each tool's clause ends in
    ;   (> (hands-clear TOOL) R)
    ; -- no hand within R of the tool's origin, R being the tool's radius about
    ; that origin plus 15 mm, rounded up to the centimetre, so a hand nearer
    ; than R could still be holding it -- and holds for a second (the wrenches'
    ; whole goal for two), so a tool sliding off as it is let go is not counted.
    ; contact-force against the holder is not a release test: a tool lowered
    ; onto its hook while still in the jaws reads well above its 0.2 N floor.
  )

  (:fixtures
    pegboard - skadis_pegboard
  )

  (:provenance
    (:tier original)
    (:source "Scenes, objects and routines ported from the tool-hanging branch at
              3e20fc7 -- goals authored here over features measured off the
              vendored meshes. Mesh licences pending confirmation -- see this
              task's assets/PROVENANCE.md.")
  )

  ; Headline first, then the four scripted families, then their one-object
  ; reductions -- the order the suite lists and the gauntlet walks.
  (:variants wrenches screwdrivers hammers scissors pliers
             wrenches_level1 screwdrivers_level1 scissors_level1 pliers_level1
             wrenches_level2 screwdrivers_level2 scissors_level2 pliers_level2)
)
